## Module 3: Guardrails

-strict_mode = true
- if strict_mode == true:
    - only include claims, equations, and results that appear in the provided text and nothing else
    - if the LLM cannot find enough information, this must be explicitly stated
if strict_mode ==false:
    -outside sources may be used
    -LLM must state when an outside source is used and cite said source

- Flag missing/empty sections.
- Flag sections <50 words.
- if a section is flagged, a standardized warning must be output regarding why the section was flagged. for example: "section skipped: no usable text available"

- Mitigate hallucinations: only summarize provided text.
- Chunk long papers into manageable segments.
